/* Strict weak ordering, the three rules:
   1. Irreflexive : cmp(a, a) must be false.
   2. Asymmetric  : if cmp(a, b) then !cmp(b, a).
   3. Transitive  : cmp(a,b) && cmp(b,c) implies cmp(a,c);
                    equivalence (neither less) must be transitive too.
   libstdc++'s introsort uses the comparator itself as the loop guard while
   partitioning. With <=, equal elements never stop the scan, the pointer runs
   past the end of the partition, and it reads unowned memory. */

